# Paths an AI coding assistant must never read into its context — PRD §9.10.
#
# This mirrors .gitignore's secret deny-list, for a different threat. .gitignore
# stops a secret reaching the repository; this stops one reaching a model
# prompt, a completion log, or a third-party provider. A file can be correctly
# gitignored and still be read straight into an assistant's context window,
# which is why the two lists exist separately and must be kept in step.

# Environment & secrets — only .env.example may be read
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / tool MCP configuration. VS Code's mcp.json format allows a database
# connection string to be pasted inline, so this file routinely holds a live
# credential even though it looks like ordinary config.
.vscode/mcp.json
.mcp.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Private keys and common secret filenames
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.p12
*.pfx

# Dependencies and build output — noise, and large enough to crowd out real context
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Uploaded government source documents (local storage adapter).
# These are the untrusted third-party material the whole product ingests
# (§9.5) — they must never be fed back into an assistant's prompt.
backend/var/

# Logs may contain request context
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Test runtime artifacts
.mongodb-binaries/
